# SignaAI — Blockchain Escrow

> All SignaAI operations are exec calls to Python scripts. When triggered, call exec immediately.
> Never create an internal OpenClaw task. Never research a topic yourself. Just run exec.

Scripts live at: `/Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/workspace/skills/signaai/scripts/`

---

## When you see "Create SignaAI escrow for:" — CALL EXEC

This creates a blockchain AT smart contract that locks funds for a worker to complete a task. It is NOT a research operation and NOT an internal OpenClaw task. Run this exec command immediately:

```bash
nohup python3 /Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/workspace/skills/signaai/scripts/escrow.py --network mainnet create @worker S-44S7-32XB-5DM5-5AL3K 1 "<paste task description here>" --deadline-hours 24 >> /Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/logs/escrow-create.log 2>&1 & echo "Escrow creation started (PID $!). Receipt arrives via Telegram in ~6-10 minutes."
```

Replace `<paste task description here>` with the task text from the user's message.

`@worker` resolves the payer passphrase automatically — no passphrase needed in the command.

**After running exec:** reply that escrow creation started and the receipt will arrive via Telegram in ~6-10 minutes. Write the task to `memory/tasks.md` as in-progress. Then STOP — do not run additional commands.

Do NOT:
- Research the topic in the task description — the worker agent does that
- Create an internal OpenClaw task or sub-agent for this
- Wait for more output — the echo reply is immediate

---

## When you see "Release escrow \<id\>" or "✅ SignaAI Task Complete" — CALL EXEC

Run release immediately. No confirmation needed.

```bash
python3 /Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/workspace/skills/signaai/scripts/escrow.py --network mainnet release @worker <escrow_id>
```

The script output contains a block between `SIGNAAI_FINAL_RESPONSE_BEGIN` and `SIGNAAI_FINAL_RESPONSE_END`. Copy the text between those markers exactly and output nothing else.

Do NOT run `escrow.py status` before release — it always returns CREATED and will block a valid release.

